 "notes": "Printed p. 288, cols 38-55. Blocks: Mother-tongue Kanarese contd. (cols 38-43: subsidiary Tamil, Telugu, Tulu; totals on leaf 293), Mother-tongue Kond (cols 44-51: total returning; subsidiary Oriya, Telugu, Hill and Aboriginal), Mother-tongue Konkani (cols 52-55: total returning; subsidiary Hindustani; block continues on leaf 295). Only Males/Females printed. Discrepancies in the print (kept as printed): (1) Kanarese/Telugu males, Madras States total printed 293 but Banganapalle 70 + Sandur 228 = 298 (Madras 79,549 = British Territory 79,256 + 293, so the 293 is consistent with the Presidency total; one of the state figures is presumably misprinted). (2) Konkani: Madras and British Territory rows print '..' in cols 52-55; only South Kanara carries figures (99,351 / 102,022; Hindustani 394 / 202). All other area totals reconcile."
